<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- GENERATED by scripts/make_bushfire_world - do not edit by hand.
     Regenerate with: rosrun uav_bushfire make_bushfire_world

     The fire ground: a stand of dry eucalypt inside a bulldozed firebreak,
     with unburnt bush beyond it, for three quadrotors to water-bomb ground
     fires in.

     WHAT IS LOAD-BEARING HERE, because most of this file is scenery and some
     of it is not:

     THE EIGHT TRUNKS IN THE STAND. At (+-2.5, +-2.5) and on the axes at 4.5,
     each with a collision cylinder of radius 0.35 and height 3.0. That list
     is duplicated in bushfire_fleet.launch as ~obstacles and read by three
     nodes - fire_spotter, so it never lights a fire inside a trunk it cannot
     see; fire_suppressor, to govern near one; collision_monitor, to score a
     strike. Move a trunk here and that file has to move with it. The
     generator prints the list and refuses to write a world where they differ.

     ONLY TRUNKS COLLIDE. Everything else on the fire ground - canopies,
     branches, roots, logs, stumps, rocks, tussocks - carries a visual and NO
     collision, and that is deliberate rather than an oversight. The laser is
     a horizontal plane on a mast: it sees trunks perfectly and cannot see
     anything above or below the aircraft. Collision geometry the laser cannot
     return would be an obstacle the drone can hit and has no sensor able to
     detect, which is the one scene fire_suppressor's own header says it
     cannot handle. Giving the trees tops a rotor passes through keeps the
     picture honest: the drone only ever collides with things it could have
     seen coming.

     THERE IS NO WALL, and that is a change from earlier versions of this
     file. Containment is fire_suppressor's geofence - soft at 4.8 m, hard at
     8.0 m where the aircraft is teleported back to its launch point. The four
     3 m walls that used to stand at +-6 made the place read as a room and
     were never the backstop they looked like: the suppressor's header records
     a drone going over one at 3.5 m and still accelerating 275 m away.

     THE SURROUNDING BUSH STARTS AT 8.8 m, OUTSIDE THAT HARD GEOFENCE. Its
     trunks do collide - they are laser-visible, so ghosts would be the
     dishonest option - but they are NOT in ~obstacles, so collision_monitor
     does not score them. They therefore have to sit where no aircraft can
     arrive. At 7.2 m they were inside the band a soft-fenced drone reaches
     and a run put uav_1 straight through them.

     TRUNK HEIGHT. 3 m against a top cruise lane of 2.60, to stop the obvious
     cheat - an aircraft's answer to an obstacle is to go over it, and if it
     can, the reactive avoidance this scenario is built around never runs.

     THE MIDDLE IS CLEAR. Three launch points on the y axis at (0, 0) and
     (0, +-2.2). No furniture within 1.1 m of any of them.

     THE FURNITURE IS OUTSIDE THE FIRE ZONE. fire_spotter lights fires within
     +-4.0 m. Logs, stumps and rocks sit beyond 4.3 m, so a fire can never be
     lit inside one. They are NOT in ~obstacles and must not be added to it:
     fire_suppressor's governor treats every entry as a full-height keep-out
     with no notion of z, so a 0.4 m log would push aircraft off course at
     cruise for something they fly over. -->
<sdf version="1.6">
  <world name="default">

    <scene>
      <ambient>0.42 0.41 0.39 1</ambient>
      <background>0.66 0.60 0.53 1</background>
      <shadows>false</shadows>
      <fog>
        <color>0.62 0.55 0.48 1</color>
        <type>linear</type>
        <start>9</start>
        <end>58</end>
        <density>0.72</density>
      </fog>
    </scene>

    <physics type="ode">
      <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>
      <real_time_update_rate>1000</real_time_update_rate>
    </physics>

    <!-- Key: low, warm, and from the north-west. Sun through smoke. -->
    <light name="sun_key" type="directional">
      <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 12 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.96 0.86 0.70 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.18 0.16 0.13 1</specular>
      <direction>0.42 0.36 -0.83</direction>
      <attenuation><range>90</range><constant>0.9</constant>
        <linear>0.01</linear><quadratic>0.001</quadratic></attenuation>
    </light>

    <!-- Fill: cool, weak, from the opposite side, and never casts. This is
         the light that keeps the underside of a crown from going black. -->
    <light name="sky_fill" type="directional">
      <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 12 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.34 0.37 0.44 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.0 0.0 0.0 1</specular>
      <direction>-0.55 -0.42 -0.72</direction>
      <attenuation><range>90</range><constant>1.0</constant>
        <linear>0.0</linear><quadratic>0.0</quadratic></attenuation>
    </light>

